      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument that a concrete, immediate tax hike is equivalent to a theoretical economic projection is a fundamental disagreement over what constitutes responsible governance. A functioning society requires both immediate fiscal stability and a vision for future growth, and the current plan fails because it prioritizes the latter at the expense of the former. Therefore, the plan is not just flawed; it is fiscally irresponsible because it ignores the immediate, guaranteed burden on existing citizens.",
      "source": "target",
